  "selected": {
    "id": "5300ddcb4d54",
    "title": "Francis I of France: The Knight King of the French Renaissance",
    "url": "https://www.worldhistory.org/Francis_I_of_France/",
    "text": "Francis I (1494-1547) reigned as King of France from 1515 until his death in 1547, at the height of the French Renaissance. A humanist, man of letters, and great lover of the arts, Francis patronized many Italian artists during his rule and transformed Paris into a hub of Renaissance art and culture. He was also known for his role in the Italian Wars (1494-1559) as well as for his rivalry with Charles V, Holy Roman Emperor. In his own lifetime and afterwards, Francis was known as le Roi-Chevalier, or the \"Knight King.\"",
    "published": "2026-11-19T10:00:02.000Z",
    "official": true,
    "dateBasis": "item_publication_or_update",
    "publisher": "www.worldhistory.org",
